# A test that needs a NUL byte in a fixture can write one as a literal, and
# git's binary heuristic then calls the whole file binary: the diff collapses to
# "Binary files differ" with no line counts, so nobody reviews it. Escape
# sequences are the fix in the source; this makes the diff readable even when a
# file slips through.
#
# `diff`, not `text diff`. `diff` alone is the part that keeps such a file
# reviewable. `text` additionally turns on end-of-line normalisation for every
# Dart file in the repo, which is a working-tree-wide change with nothing to do
# with reviewable diffs.
*.dart diff
